@node D-Bus Elisp API
@section Elisp API

Every DEFUN provided by cmacs's D-Bus subsystem.  All are autoloaded
when @option{--with-cmacs-glib} is enabled at configure time.

@subsection Lifecycle

@table @code
@item (cmacs-dbus-start)
Connect to the session bus, register all enabled interface modules
at @code{/org/cmacs/Editor}, claim the well-known and per-PID
names.  Returns the dominant bus name (well-known if acquired, else
the per-PID fallback).  Idempotent.

@item (cmacs-dbus-stop)
Tear down the registration.  Returns @code{t} if the service was
running, @code{nil} otherwise.

@item (cmacs-dbus-name)
Dominant bus name (well-known if held, else per-PID).  @code{nil}
when stopped.

@item (cmacs-dbus-well-known-name)
The well-known name @code{org.cmacs.Editor} if this cmacs holds it;
@code{nil} if another cmacs already owned it when we started, or if
we're stopped.

@item (cmacs-dbus-per-pid-name)
The per-PID name @code{org.cmacs.Editor.Pid@var{N}} (always claimed
when running), or @code{nil} when stopped.
@end table

@subsection Signal emission

@table @code
@item (cmacs-dbus-emit-signal PATH IFACE NAME &optional PARAMS)
Emit a D-Bus signal at @var{PATH} on @var{IFACE} named @var{NAME}.
@var{PARAMS} is a list whose elements are auto-marshalled into a
tuple of best-fit GVariant types.  Returns @code{t} on success,
@code{nil} if the service is not running (no-op in that case).
Never raises.

Example:
@example
(cmacs-dbus-emit-signal
 "/org/cmacs/Editor"
 "org.example.MyApp"
 "Heartbeat"
 (list "alive" 42))
@end example

@item (cmacs-dbus-emit-properties-changed PATH IFACE CHANGED &optional INVALIDATED)
Emit the standard
@code{org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties.PropertiesChanged} signal.
@var{CHANGED} is a plist; @var{INVALIDATED} is a list of property
names.

Example:
@example
(cmacs-dbus-emit-properties-changed
 "/org/cmacs/Editor/Buffer/12"
 "org.cmacs.Editor1.Buffer.Resource"
 (list :modified t :point 1234) nil)
@end example
@end table

@subsection Customization

Phase 1 has no defcustoms; the surface is on / off via
@code{cmacs-dbus-start} / @code{cmacs-dbus-stop}.  Phases 4 and 5
will add opt-in customizations.

@subsection Patterns

@subsubheading Conditional emit

The emit DEFUNs no-op when the service is stopped, so it's safe to
unconditionally call them from hooks even if the user hasn't started
the service:

@example
(cmacs-dbus-emit-signal "/org/cmacs/Editor"
                        "org.example.App" "Tick" '("hello"))
@end example

@subsubheading Forwarding hook events as signals

@example
(dolist (hook '(after-save-hook
                kill-buffer-hook
                find-file-hook))
  (add-hook hook
    (lambda (&rest _)
      (cmacs-dbus-emit-signal
       "/org/cmacs/Editor"
       "org.cmacs.Editor1.Hooks"
       (symbol-name hook) nil))))
@end example

External tools then watch
@command{gdbus monitor --session --dest org.cmacs.Editor} to react
to editor activity in real time.
